Step by Step Algorithm: 

Step 1: Initialize curr = 0 and tot = -∞.
Step 2: Traverse the array from left to right.
Step 3: For each element, update
        curr = max(nums[i], curr + nums[i]).
Step 4: Update maximum sum
        tot = max(tot, curr).
Step 5: Continue until the end of the array.
Step 6: Return tot as the maximum subarray sum.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)


-----> Code <------


class Solution {
    public int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        int curr=0,tot=Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            curr=Math.max(curr+nums[i],nums[i]);
            tot=Math.max(curr,tot);
        }
        return tot;
    }
}
